## 3. HYPOTHESIS

> Generated reasoning, not evidence. Do not cite as fact. Do not promote without experimental or clinical validation.

### H1 — Vaccine Timing Window

**Claim:** Administering STC-1010 during the bevacizumab CD8+ vascular normalization window (~cycle 2, days 14–28) would improve vaccine-driven T-cell priming relative to arbitrary scheduling.

**Basis:** Bevacizumab normalization window literature (PMIDs 36858688, 24399798, 28698619) + Agent 5 line 53 analytical interpretation. No clinical data for STC-1010 timing optimization exists.

**Label:** [MECHANISTIC HYPOTHESIS — generated reasoning, not evidence]

---

### H2 — HT29 BRAF V600E Antigen Axis

**Claim:** HT29's BRAF V600E / KRAS-WT antigen component introduces a non-KRAS immune axis into STC-1010 that may be relevant to the Morris Cancer Cell 2025 BRAF V600E MSS ORR signal (50% ORR, n=26, NCT04017650, PMID 40882637).

**Basis:** HT29 cell line biology (ATCC/CCLE) + Morris Cancer Cell 2025 (cited in Agent 4) + P2.1 (cell line identity provisional). Depends on P2.1 being confirmed.

**Label:** [HYPOTHESIS — contingent on P2.1 verification; generated reasoning, not evidence]

---

### H3 — TCGA Re-Scoping

**Claim:** TCGA-COAD/READ analysis scoped to KRAS G13D (HCT116, LoVo) + BRAF V600E / KRAS-WT (HT29) MSS patients would produce a more precise comparator population for STC-1010 biomarker analysis than "KRAS-mutant MSS" broadly.

**Basis:** P2.1 (cell line identity) + HT29 BRAF V600E status (VERIFIED). Depends on P2.1 being confirmed.

**Label:** [HYPOTHESIS — contingent on P2.1 verification; generated reasoning, not evidence]

---

### H4 — Bevacizumab 2-Day Pre-Cytotoxic Gap

**Claim:** Administering bevacizumab ~2 days before chemotherapy yields better efficacy than concomitant dosing via transient vascular normalization → improved drug uptake.

**Basis:** General vascular normalization window literature [46, 49, 51, 53]. Specific "2-day" timing claim not retrieved from a primary source in this session.

**Label:** [HYPOTHESIS — specific timing claim unverified; do not cite as fact]

---

### H5 — Composite Highest-Benefit Subgroup

**Claim:** The STC-1010 highest-benefit subgroup is: MSS + no active liver metastases + SMAD4 intact + low TGF-β exclusion signature + KRAS-WT or BRAF V600E (~10–20% of MSS mCRC).

**Basis:** Agent 4 §5 Priority Stratification Hypothesis; Agent 3 Synthesis Memo §2 (biomarker subgroup structures). No clinical validation for STC-1010 exists.

**Label:** [MECHANISTIC HYPOTHESIS — Agent 4; generated reasoning from literature synthesis, not clinical evidence]

